    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45698" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">styrax</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">stŏrax</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Sol. 33 <i>med.</i></span></i>; <i><span class="en">Isid. Orig.
			17, 8, 5</span></i>), ăcis, m., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στύραξ</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a tree; and also the resinous gum of that
				tree</i>, <i>storax</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 12,
				25, 55, § 125</span></i>; <i><span class="en">24, 6, 15, §
			24</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. Cir.
			167</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">styrăcĭnus</span></b> , a,
				um, <i>of</i> or <i>made from
				storax</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oleum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cael.
					Aur. Tard. 2, 7</span></i>
			.</div>
